      "rationale": "All three combination shapes the competency allows are produced: bills only, coins only, and mixtures such as 1 ₱50 bill, 2 ₱10 coins, and 1 ₱1 coin. Denominations stay clear of centavo pieces as the exclusion requires."
    },
    "cognitive_capacity": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Piece counts stay at three or fewer per denomination and the totals are reached by adding a handful of friendly amounts, which suits fourth-quarter Grade 1 money work."
    },
    "variant_comprehensiveness": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "The value items differ only in their opening verb, cycling between finding the total amount, asking what the total value is, and determining the total value, while the underlying sentence shape never changes. No purchase, change-giving, or comparison-of-two-purses context appears anywhere in the set."
    },
    "competency_alignment": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Harder samples add more denominations to the pile, moving from a single pair of like pieces up to a four-denomination mixture, so the rising demand is exactly the demand of totalling assorted money."
    },
    "scale_appropriateness": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Totals reach ₱100 exactly and never exceed it. The tenfold distractors such as 710 against a key of 71 are far outside any plausible money value, though they do not breach the competency's stated ceiling for the keys themselves."
